 "."
}], "Usage",
 CellID->811,ExpressionUUID->"16a1e11b-8a71-463e-a6bf-dfdabdec967e"],

Cell["\<\
Compute[sol[object, key, $auto, autoKey]] computes the components of autoKey \
by walking the Chain stored under its Routine, and records the result under \
Value so that it survives SaveData.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->812,ExpressionUUID->"a69ee53c-697a-490f-be4c-83a9f2a098e2"],

Cell["\<\
Compute[sol[object, key]] does this for every automatic tensor of the entry.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->813,ExpressionUUID->"fde9c947-87d8-48f3-8961-7b5b4c4900c0"],

Cell["\<\
A Chain entry of the form HoldForm[expr] -> {slots} evaluates expr, with \
$self standing for the solution, and takes it as the components for those \
index slots. An entry of the form {slots} -> {slots} obtains the right-hand \
slots from the left-hand ones by raising or lowering with the metric. In a \
slot specification -1 is a lowered index and 1 a raised one.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->814,ExpressionUUID->"f4a05e95-d31a-4821-8fb1-dda91ffd8eff"],

Cell["\<\
A raising entry gives values to the components that are independent within \
each slot configuration it computes, and to no others. Canonicalizing a \
mixed-index component of a tensor with symmetries can carry the raised index \
to a different slot, and such a component resolves only if the configuration \
of its representative is also in the Chain. This is deliberate: Compute does \
exactly what the Chain names, so the user decides what is computed and when. \
Raise through the full permutation orbit of each level, as in the example \
below, when every arrangement of the indices should resolve; a partial chain \
is legitimate whenever only the computed configurations are wanted.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->815,ExpressionUUID->"364040eb-c075-44c7-9dd6-f832d8cf6d3b"],

Cell["\<\
Nothing is computed if the Chain is unset, which is its initial state. \
Compute is silent in that case. The one exception is the companion tensor of \
a differential form, which is given a chain automatically when the form is \
included.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->816,ExpressionUUID->"0b790e00-e486-412e-ae98-be1e44d38781"],

Cell["\<\
Components of a differential form are normally computed with Apply -> {Map -> \
Identity}, since simplifying a wedge product is rarely what is wanted.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->817,ExpressionUUID->"1f66a13f-3805-45a2-a959-a521f40fec15"],

Cell["\<\
The option Chain overrides the stored recipe and stores the one given. The \
option Using chooses the metric used for each bundle, and defaults to the \
first metric of that bundle. The option Apply defaults to $Apply.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->818,ExpressionUUID->"d20d19be-2baa-4042-a883-e51d8d5d474b"],

Cell["\<\
Because the recipe is stored beside the answer, a saved solution can always \
be recomputed from scratch rather than merely trusted.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->819,ExpressionUUID->"1382a8e2-ce4f-4b40-addf-f5086c71a629"],

Cell["Compute has the attribute HoldFirst.", "Notes",
 CellID->820,ExpressionUUID->"f7ed2144-3c5b-4a9f-a9bf-a7931274b466"]
}, Open  ]],

